            <ArticleTitle>Incarcerated tubal herniation, an unusual complication of operative laparoscopy and an odd cause of pelvic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>159-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tubal herniation after laparoscopic surgery to relieve pelvic pain and adhesions was associated with long-term, chronic pelvic pain in the left lower quadrant. Laparoscopy was performed to diagnose and reduce the herniation. Review of the literature revealed no previous report of this complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
